<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottonian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">919–1024</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Liudolfings, Liudolfing dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottonian dynasty, also called the Liudolfings, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> family that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, from 919 to 1024. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> was the first king, and his son Otto I defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> at the Lechfeld in 955 and was crowned emperor in 962. Otto II, Otto III and Henry II followed. Their reign saw a flowering of art and learning known as the Ottonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>.</p></div>
